am L51:     * cite39†Master Program L52:     * cite40†Doctoral Program L53:   * Non-degree/Foundation Program\nL54: \nL55:     * cite41†Chinese Language Program L56:     * cite42†International Foundation Program L57:     * cite43†Student Exchange Program L58:     * cite44†Visiting Scholar Program L59:     * cite45†Summer Camp L60:     * cite46†Short-Term Programs L61:   * cite47†English-taught Programs L62: cite48†Image current location: cite4†HOME > cite49†Programs > cite50†Non-degree/Foundation Program > cite42†International Foundation Program > Content International Foundation Program\nL63: # 2027 Pre-university Foundation Programs of Xi'an Jiaotong University（Chinese-taught）\nL64: ##\nL65: \nL66: Release time :2026-09-30 Click-throughput：\nL67: \nL68: 2027 Pre-university Foundation Programs of\nL69: \nL70: Xi’an Jiaotong University （Chinese-taught）\nL71: Xi'an Jiaotong University (XJTU), founded in 1896, is a national key university directly under the administration of China's Ministry of Education.\nL72: As one of China's top ten research-intensive universities and a member of the C9 League—China's equivalent of the Ivy League—it operates as a comprehensive research university, encompassing 11 major disciplinary categories, including science, engineering, medicine, economics, management, humanities, law, philosophy, art, education, and interdisciplinary studies. A total of 4,484 international students from 128 countries and regions are enrolled at XJTU.\nL73: In 2013, the university was designated by China's Ministry of Education as a “Demonstration Base for International Education”. In 2024, XJTU achieved the highest rating of Class A+ in the re-certification of higher education quality for international students in China. In the 202 6 Best Chinese Universities Ranking, XJTU secured the 10^{th} position.\nL74: Program Introduction\nL75: \nL76: International Foundation Program (IFP)\nL77: \nL78: XJTU offers International Foundation Programs (11/18/36 weeks) to high school and holders of equivalent academic qualifications to help them enhance their competitiveness for admission to prestigious universities.\nL79: \nL80: cite51†Image L81: \nL82: “1+4” Foundation-Bachelor Program\nL83: XJTU offers “1+4” Foundation-Bachelor Program (11/18/36 weeks) for outstanding high school and holders of equivalent academic qualifications, aiming to help applicants advance their knowledge structure. Applicants will be assessed for their eligibility for undergraduate studies through a comprehensive review during the Foundation Program application phase.\nL84: Upon successful completion of the foundation program, students who have demonstrated Chinese language proficiency equivalent to Level 4 of the Chinese Language Proficiency Scales for Speakers of Other Languages (HSK 4) and submitted a qualifying score report of the China Scholastic Competency Assessment (CSCA) shall be deemed eligible for direct admission to undergraduate programs.\nL85: cite52†Image L86: Note: All applicants for undergraduate degree programs in China are required to take the \"China Scholastic Competency Assessment (CSCA)\" —administered by the China Scholarship Council on behalf of the Ministry of Education of the People’s Republic of China— and submit a valid score report. For detailed information and registration procedures please refer to the official CSCA website (www.csca.cn).\nL87: The specific test subjects required for each undergraduate program at Xi’an Jiaotong University are available on the official website of Xi’an Jiaotong University:\nL88: (https://sie.xjtu.edu.cn/en/Programs/Degree_Program/Bachelor_Program.htm).\nL89: \nL90: Program Features\nL91: \nL92: The International Foundation Program Center, School of International Education of Xi’an Jiaotong University offers a wide variety of customized courses for international students who are planning to pursue Chinese-taught bachelor degrees in China. It equips students with the necessary preparation for further academic pursuits within a dynamic and supportive university environment.\nL93: The center implements small-class teaching, with students divided into classes based on their intended majors and current Chinese language proficiency. Through 36-week, 18-week, or 11-week program formats, the program is designed to help international students develop foundational Chinese language skills, academic Chinese tailored to specific disciplines, core subject knowledge, and cross-cultural communication competence—laying a solid groundwork for their subsequent degree studies.\nL94: Additionally, the center provides international students with a suite of guidance services, such as visa application assistance, consultations on admission and scholarship policies, guidance on application procedures, lectures on university academic life, and recommendations for partner universities. These services create favorable conditions to facilitate international students’ successful enrollment in Chinese universities.\nL95: \nL96: Eligibility\nL97: U nder the age of 24 & with good health status (Guardian authorization is required for those under 18 years old)\nL98: \nL99: Valid ordinary passport\nL100: \nL101: High school/ senior secondary diploma or equivalent (Graduating students can apply with their transcript of mock examination）\nL102: \nL103: Grades and Chinese language proficiency requirements\nL104: Program Name  | Length of Program  | Field of Study  | Chinese language proficiency  | High School Grades\nL105:  |\nL106:  |\nL107:  |\nL108:  | IFP  | “1+4”\nL109: Basic Program  | 36 weeks  | Humanities (Business& Social Science),Science& Engineering  | None  | Average of 60% in High School  | Average of 70% in High School\nL110: Advanced Program  | 18 weeks  |\nL111:  | HSK2~3 or equivalent  |\nL112:  |\nL113: Intensive Program  | 11 weeks  |\nL114:  | HSK4 or above or equivalent  |\nL115:  |\nL116: \nL117: Start Time & Application Deadline\nL118: Program  | Start Time  | Application Deadline\nL119: Basic Program  | September, 2027  | November 1, 2026-July 15, 2027\nL120: Advanced Program  | February, 2027  | October 1, 2026-January 15, 2027\nL121: Intensive Program  | April, 2027  | October 1, 2026-March 12, 2027\nL122: \nL123: Tuition Fee\nL124: \nL125: Foundation Programs (Unit: RMB)\nL126: \nL127: Field of Study  | 36 weeks  | 18 weeks  | 11 weeks\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n西南交通大学2027学年语言生项目招生简章-西南交通大学国际教育学院 (https://sie.swjtu.edu.cn/info/1014/3352.htm)\nciteturn35view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn34view3\",\"lineno\":45}); Total lines: 194\nL0: cite0†在线申请†admission.swjtu.edu.cn L1: \nL2: cite1†ENGLISH L3: \nL4:   * cite2†关于我们 L5: \nL6:     * cite2†学院简介 L7:     * cite3†工作人员 L8: \nL9:   * cite4†招生信息 L10: \nL11:     * cite4†学历学位项目 L12:     * cite5†非学历项目 L13:     * cite6†奖学金 L14:     * cite7†导师信息 L15: \nL16:   * cite8†教育教学 L17: \nL18:     * cite8†本科生 L19:     * cite9†研究生 L20:     * cite10†语言生 L21:     * cite11†语言文化项目 L22: \nL23:   * cite12†校园生活 L24: \nL25:     * cite12†城市简介 L26:     * cite13†交通信息 L27:     * cite14†报到须知 L28:     * cite15†证照办理 L29:     * cite16†住宿指引 L30:     * cite17†网络通信 L31:     * cite18†保险指南 L32:     * cite19†生活指南 L33:     * cite20†规章制度 L34:     * cite21†学生活动 L35: \nL36:   * cite22†学前准备 L37: \nL38:     * cite22†到校前指南 L39:     * cite23†法律法规 L40: \nL41:   * cite24†出国留学 L42:     * cite24†培训简介 L43:     * cite25†培训新闻 L44: \nL45:   * cite26†校友网络 L46: \nL47:     * cite26†校友网络 L48:     * cite27†与学校链接 L49: \nL50:   * cite28†下载中心 L51: \nL52:     * cite28†行前准备 L53:     * cite29†教学相关 L54:     * cite30†毕业、结业相关 L55:     * cite31†签证相关 L56:     * cite32†住宿相关 L57: \nL58: 通知公告\nL59: \nL60: cite33†首页 > cite34†通知公告 > 正文\nL61: ###### 通知公告\nL62: \nL63: 西南交通大学2027学年语言生项目招生简章\nL64: \nL65: 西南交通大学是教育部直属全国重点大学，国家首批“双一流”、“211工程”、“985工程优势学科创新平台”、“2011协同创新计划”重点建设高校，设有研究生院，坐落于中国历史文化名城、国家中心城市、“成渝地区双城经济圈”核心城市——成都。\nL66: \nL67: 西南交通大学的语言生项目专注于汉语学习和中国文化体验。西南交通大学国际教育学院每学期都为不同汉语水平的国际学生开设多种汉语课程和文化课程。学生根据入学测试结果参加相应层级的班级学习。经验丰富的教师和小班教学将确保获得良好的教学效果。\nL68: \nL69: 一、申请日期\nL70: \nL71: 春季入学申请即日起至2027年1月1日；秋季入学申请从2027年3月1日起至2027年6月30日。\nL72: \nL73: 注：春季学期从3月至7月，秋季学期从9月至12月。\nL74: \nL75: 二、项目信息\nL76: \nL77: 1. 授课语言：英文+中文\nL78: \nL79: 2. 项目目标：\nL80: \nL81: 初级班：通过HSK3级；中级班：通过HSK4/5级\nL82: \nL83: 3. 项目时长：\nL84: \nL85: 初级班：2学期；中级班：1学期\nL86: \nL87: 4. 费用：\nL88: \nL89: a.报名费：400元/人\nL90: \nL91: b.保险：1000元/人/年\nL92: c.学费：7000元/人/学期，14000元/人/学年\nL93: \nL94: d.住宿费：365元/月/人（犀浦校区留学生公寓两人卧室，不含水电费）。\nL95: \nL96: 注：报名费恕不退还。一旦课程开始，所有费用将不予退还；学生可以住在校外，也可以在有条件的情况下申请校内公寓。\nL97: \nL98: 三、申请条件\nL99: \nL100: 1. 非中国籍公民，身心健康；遵守中华人民共和国法律法规和学校规章制度，无违法违纪记录。\nL101: \nL102: 2. 申请人年龄需17-50周岁；\nL103: \nL104: 3. 申请人应能负担项目期间在华学习和生活费用；\nL105: \nL106: 四、申请网站\nL107: \nL108: 西南交通大学：https://admission.swjtu.edu.cn\nL109: \nL110: 注：申请春季入学的申请人应在2027年1月1日前完成网上申请，申请秋季入学的申请人应在2027年6月30日前完成网上申请，申请费400元（不退还）。\nL111: \nL112: 五、申请材料及申请流程\nL113: \nL114: （一）申请材料请详见附件1\nL115: \nL116: （二）申请流程\nL117: \nL118: 1. 学校系统申请（非常重要）：请在学校申请系统(cite35†https://admission.swjtu.edu.cn)中提交申请†admission.swjtu.edu.xn--cn)-x68d9uh03hipzec2b 。\nL119: 2. 学校初审：学校按照招生要求，对申请人资格进行初审。初审合格的申请人须缴纳申请费人民币400元。无论是否录取，申请费不予退还。\nL120: \nL121: 3. 发放录取通知书：录取后，学校将提供《录取通知书》及签证申请表（DQ/JW202）等文件。\nL122: \nL123: 六、其他事项\nL124: \nL125: 1. 申请人必须确保申请材料的真实性，一经查实材料不实，将取消申请人资格。\nL126: \nL127: 2. 所有申请须在线提交，不接受电子邮件申请或纸质材料申请。\nL128: \nL129: 3. 请务必提供正确的电子邮件地址和邮寄地址。我们将通过电子邮件确认每项重要信息，请务必每天查看。\nL130: \nL131: 4. 在读期间，须遵守中华人民共和国的法律、法规和西南交通大学的校纪、校规。若学生出现违法、违纪或违规行为，学校将按相关规定处理，所有后果由学生本人承担。\nL132: \nL133: 5. 该简章最终解释权归西南交通大学国际教育学院所有。\nL134: \nL135: 七、联系方式\nL136: \nL137: 联系电话：028-66366920 (北京时间：上午8：30-12:00；下午2:00-5:30）\nL138: \nL139: 电子邮件：sie@swjtu.edu.cn\nL140: \nL141: 网站：https://en.swjtu.edu.cn\nL142: \nL143:              https://sie.swjtu.edu.cn\nL144: 附件：语言生项目申请材料说明\nL145: \nL146: Application Documents Requirements for Chinese Language Learning Programs\nL147: \nL148: 1. 护照首页扫描件Scanned Copy of Passport Home Page. 如现持有护照有效期不符合要求(护照有效期应晚于 2027 年 9 月)，请及时换发新护照。If the validity of the applicant’s current passport does not meet the requirement (meaning the passport expires before September 2027), please apply for a new passport before submitting the application.\nL149: 2. 经公证的学历证明Notarized academic certificate. 如果文件不是英文或中文，请提供经过公证的翻译件。Please provide notarized translation if the documents are not in English or Chinese.\nL150: \nL151: 3. 成绩单Academic Records. 如果文件不是英文或中文，请提供经过公证的翻译件。Please provide notarized translation if the documents are not in English or Chinese.\nL152: 4. 《外国人体格检查表》扫描件。Scanned copy of the Foreigner Physical Examination Form. 申请人须保存原始体检表。本表由中国卫生检疫部门统一印制，需用英文填写，可以从https://en.swjtu.edu.cn/FOREIGNER_PHYSICAL_EXAMINAT_ON_FORM.pdf下载。体检必须包括《外国人体格检查表》所列的所有项目。不完整、无主治医生签名、无医院公章、无申请人盖章的照片，均视为无效。体检结果有效期仅为6个月，请慎重安排体检时间。The original form should be kept by the applicant. The form is uniformly printed by Chinese healthy quarantine departments.\nL153: It must be written in English and can be downloaded from cite36†https://en.swjtu.edu.cn/FOREIGNER_PHYSICAL_EXAMINAT_ON_FORM.pdf†en.swjtu.edu.cn . The physical examinations must cover all of the items listed in the Foreigner Physical Examination Form. Incomplete forms or forms without the signature of the attending physician, or the official stamp of the hospital, or a sealed photograph of the applicant are considered as invalid.\nL154: Please carefully plan your physical examination schedule as the result is valid for only 6 months.\nL155: 5. 由银行出具的申请人的对账单、存款证明或担保人签署的担保证明。Applicant’s Bank Statement or Certificate of Deposit or the statement of financial support signed by sponsor.\nL156: \nL157: 它必须涵盖在中国学习所需的学费和生活费。It must cover the tuition fees and living expense needed for study in China.\nL158: 6.无犯罪记录证明Non-criminal record report. 申请人须提交由所在地公安机关出具的有效期内的无犯 罪记录证明，通常应为提交申请之日前 6 个月以内的证明文件。The applicant shall submit a valid certificate of on-Criminal Record issued by the local public security authority, usually issued within 6 months prior to the submission date of the application.\nL159: \nL160: 7. 未满18周岁的申请人须提交其在中国境内委托法定监护人的相关法律文件。Applicants under the age of 18 shall submit relevant legal documents of his/her entrusted legal guardians in China.\nL161: 8. 有效签证页Valid visa page. 目前在中国境内的申请人，应提供其当前签证或居留许可页复印件。Applicants who are in China currently should provide a copy of the page of his/her current visa or residence permit.\nL162: \nL163: 注意:通过系统上传的材料须清晰、真实、有效。建议申请人使用专业设备扫描需提交的有关文件，因材料不清晰或无法识别造成的后果由申请人承担。Reminder: Uploaded supporting documents must be clear, authentic and valid. Applicants are recommended to use a professional device to scan the relevant documents. Applicants shall bear the consequences caused by unclear or unidentifiable uploaded materials.\nL164: 犀浦校区 Xipu Campus\nL165: \nL166: cite37†Image cite38†Image cite39†Image L167: \nL168: cite40†Image cite41†Image cite42†Image L169: \nL170: 留学交大The campus life of International students\nL171: \nL172: 犀浦校区留学生公寓（鸿哲斋11栋）和超过7处的学生食堂\nL173: \nL174: The international student apartment (Building 11, Hongzhezhai) and over 7 student canteens in Xipu Campus\nL175: \nL176: cite43†Image L177: \nL178: cite44†Image cite45†Image cite46†Image L179: \nL180: cite47†Image cite48†Image cite37†Image cite49†Image cite50†Image cite51†Image L181: \nL182: 下一条:cite52†讲座：人工智能理论与实践 L183: \nL184: 版权所有：西南交通大学国际教育学院\nL185: \nL186: 地址：中国四川省成都市郫都区犀安路 999 号（邮编：611756）\nL187: ###### 相关链接\nL188: \nL189:   * cite53†西南交通大学†www.swjtu.edu.cn L190:   * cite54†西南交通大学国际合作与交流处†fad.swjtu.edu.cn L191:   * cite55†国家留学基金管理委员会†www.csc.edu.cn L192:   * cite56†教育部留学服务中心†www.cscse.edu.cn L193:   * cite57†成都市公安局出入境管理局†cdcrj.chengdu.gov.cn --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNotice on Degree Programs Application for International Students Spring Enrollment, 2027-留学生教育学院 (https://iie-en.gdufs.edu.cn/info/1174/2795.htm)\nciteturn35view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn34view4\",\"lineno\":20}); Total lines: 76\nL0: cite0†Image: 留学生学院英文主页 L1:  |\nL2: cite1† Home  cite2†Image cite3† About IIE  cite2†Image cite3† Admissions  cite2†Image cite3† HSK  cite2†Image cite3† Scholarship  cite2†Image cite3† News  cite2†Image cite3† Events  cite2†Image cite4† Download  cite2†Image cite5† Contact  cite2†Image cite6† Map †maps.google.com L3: cite7† About Guangzhou  L4: cite8† History of IIE  L5: cite9† Faculty  L6: cite10† Old Photos †iie.gdufs.edu.cn L7: cite11† Alumni  L8: cite12† IIE-LOGO  L9: cite13† Undergraduate  L10: cite14† Postgraduate  L11: cite15† Doctorate  L12: cite16† Chinese Language Training  L13: cite17† About HSK  L14: cite18† Test Center Location  L15: cite19† Application  L16: cite20† Chinese Government Scholarship  L17: cite21† International Chinese Language Teachers Scholarship  L18: cite22† Guangdong Province Government International Student Scholarship  L19: cite23† GDUFS Scholarship  L20: cite24† Application  L21: cite25† Previous Winners List  L22: cite26† Latest  L23: cite27† Anouncements  L24: cite28† Teaching Affairs  L25: cite29† Rules & Regulations  L26: cite30† Facilities  L27: cite31† Excellent Student Works  L28: cite32† Campus Environment  L29: cite33† Guangzhou Landscape  L30: cite34† Chinese Culture  L31: cite35† Campus Map  L32: cite36† Guangzhou City Map  L33: cite37† Guangzhou Metro Map  L34: Position: cite1†Home > cite38†Enrollment > cite39†Prospectus > Content\nL35:   * cite39† Prospectus  L36: cite40† Programmes  L37: cite41† Registration  L38: cite42† Visa  L39: cite43† Living Facilities  L40: cite44† Online Application  L41:  |\nL42: cite45†Image L43: Prospectus\nL44: Notice on Degree Programs Application for International Students Spring Enrollment, 2027\nL45: 2026-10-10 11:58\nL46: Application Period From September 30 to December 10, 2026. *Any change in the actual application time, please refer to the further notice of the Institute for International Education. How to apply Online application.\nL47: Applicants please submit online application through http://gdufs.17gz.org/ and please get confirmation via phone call (0086-20-36207141, 36207142) or Email (studyiniie@gdufs.edu.cn) to the Admission Office, Institute for International Education (IIE).Eligibility To be eligible, an applicant must:(1) Be non-Chinese nationality, hold a foreign passport and meet the relevant requirements of the Regulation No.〔2020〕12 by Ministry of Education of the People’s Republic of China.(2) Stay in good health both mentally and physically, and meet the physical examination standards for the study visa or residence permit in China required by the Chinese government.(3) Abide by Chinese laws and regulations and the University rules and regulations; be diligent and well-performed in academics and good conduct; no violation of the University rules and disciplines, no public security punishment, no criminal record.(4) The educational background, academic performance, language proficiency, and CSCA scores must meet the requirements for the program to which they are applying..(5) Under the age of 30 for the undergraduate programs, under the age of 35 for the postgraduate programs and under the age of 40 for the doctoral programs in principle.(6) Abide by requirements of other relevant laws and regulations.\nL48: Degree Programs and Documentation Requirements Undergraduate Programs:Chinese B. A program and Chinese (Business Chinese) program especially for international students by IIE: https://iie-en.gdufs.edu.cn/info/1132/2191.htm .Documents required for online application: 1. High school certificate and transcript. The notarized Chinese or English version must be provided if the originals are in other languages.2. Test results of the China Scholastic Competency Assessment (CSCA). Required Subjects:cite46†Image 3.\nL49: Chinese-taught Programs: Photocopy of HSK Level 5 certificate with 180 points or above, and in additional：(1) Take the necessary entrance examination, mainly in the form of: written test + interview, or interview only.(2) Chinese B.A programs: applicants for the 1st year of the Chinese B.A programs are not required to submit an HSK certificate when applying, but must have a Chinese language proficiency equivalent to HSK Level 3; simultaneously, those seeking entry into the 2nd year must provide an HSK Level 4 score of 180 points or above, and applicants for 3rd year Chinese(Business Chinese) must provide an HSK Level 5 score of 180 points or above .4.\nL50: English-taught Programs: Applicants must hold a TOEFL score of 70 or an IELTS score of 5.5 or above, and in additional：(1) Take the necessary entrance examination, mainly in the form of: written test + interview, or interview only.(2) Those who fail to provide TOEFL or IELTS certificates must pass the entrance examination organized by the institute in the format of written exam and interview.\nL51: Applicants from English-speaking countries can be exempted from the written examination, but are still required to attend an interview.(3) For applications to English-taught programs, Chinese language proficiency and HSK is not mandatory, but it is required that the HSK Level 4 exam be passed prior to graduation.5. Photocopy of passport main page and Chinese visa page (*if any), and a 1-inch digital bareheaded colorized photo.6. Valid medical examination report.7.\nL52: Any additional materials required by the University as per separate notifications, such as recommendation letter, Non-Criminal Record Certificate and ect. Please refer to Appendix 3. [GDUFS] Notice on Other Supplementary Materials.Admission The admission results are expected to be released gradually from mid-to-late January 2027.\nL53: Please kindly note: the admission results displayed in the online application system only represent the university's preliminary review opinions or intended admission, and the final admission results are subject to the official email notification of the University.Contacts Address: Office 102, Mingede No. 7^{th }Academic Building, Guangdong University of Foreign Studies, No.\nL54: 2^{nd }Baiyun Avenue North, Baiyun District, Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province PR China (Institute for International Education)Zip code: 510420 Contacts: 0086-20-36207141, 36207142 E-mail: studyiniie@gdufs.edu.cn (studyiniie@gdufs.edu.cn。)Wexin Official Account: GDUFSIIE\nL55: Appendix 1. [GDUFS] List of Tuition Fees of Degree Programs for International Students Appendix 2. [GDUFS] Online Application Guidance for International Degree Students Appendix 3. [GDUFS] Notice on China Scholastic Competency Assessment (CSCA) ＆Other Supplementary Materials\nL56: Appendix 1. [GDUFS] List of Tuition Fees of Degree Programs for International Studentscite47†Image L57: Appendix 2. [GDUFS] Online Application Guidance for International Degree Studentscite48†Image cite49†Image cite50†Image --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2027 Spring Intake Chinese Language Program 2027年春季学期/学年汉语进修项目 (https://ices.fudan.edu.cn/_t326/69/08/c6658a485640/page.htm)\nciteturn35view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn34view5\",\"lineno\":0}); Total lines: 38\nL0: cite0†中文†www.ices.fudan.edu.cn |English\nL1: \nL2: (频道)\nL3: \nL4: 2027 Spring Intake Chinese Language Program 2027年春季学期/学年汉语进修项目\nL5: \nL6: 发布时间： 2026-10-13     文章作者：     访问次数： 57521\nL7: \nL8: 详细信息请参阅项目简章 cite1†Image cite2†2027年春季外国留学生汉语进修项目招生简章.pdf L9: \nL10: Please find details cite1†Image cite3†2027 Spring Intake ICES Seme